  ### Step 1: Analyze the Architecture
  First, inspect the provided source code files to understand the layout of the application:

  • main.go is the Go gateway running on port 8080.
  • app.py is the Flask backend running on port 8081.
  • The external user can only interact with the Go gateway (port 8080), which proxies allowed requests to the Python backend.
